                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "279d9ae6-5a7b-3186-ab6f-9a58b1d0747c",
                        "entry_id": "f0e62f85-5156-302f-8de8-e11721b5c503",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To enclose in a shell."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "literary",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c28ce8a2-8434-442d-be69-39b577cc15e9",
                                "sense_id": "279d9ae6-5a7b-3186-ab6f-9a58b1d0747c",
                                "text": "’Tis Aufidius,\nWho, hearing of our Coriolanus’ banishment,\nThrusts forth his horns again into the world;\nWhich were inshell’d when Coriolanus stood for Rome,\nAnd durst not once peep out."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "530fa8b2-c166-4a62-ba5b-fb0b1d1fb605",
                                "sense_id": "279d9ae6-5a7b-3186-ab6f-9a58b1d0747c",
                                "text": "[…] of all men that I have ever known, no one was more reluctant to creep out of the modesty in which he had inshelled himself, than the man whom I cannot even yet think no more, feeling towards his memory as if he were still waiting for something not received."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ed15c37-da0e-4f66-ae54-6ccc3bfa2341",
                                "sense_id": "279d9ae6-5a7b-3186-ab6f-9a58b1d0747c",
                                "text": "Vermilion wings, by distance held\nTo pause aflight while fleeting swift:\nAnd high aloft the pearl inshelled\nHer lucid glow in glow will lift:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01f4a191-5260-4a77-bae1-67bfd780840b",
                                "sense_id": "279d9ae6-5a7b-3186-ab6f-9a58b1d0747c",
                                "text": "Who could know what forces those two-meter hulls inshelled, or what fleets and empires waited on their signal?"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
